WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.380
- [Narrator] This Sweetgreen
salad starts at 14.95.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.323
Add avocado and it goes to 16.95.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:11.340
But even as it's sold millions
of these bowls to customers,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.970
Sweetgreen has been losing
millions of dollars a month.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.380
With over 200 locations,

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.240
Sweetgreen is a fast casual restaurant

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.860
trying to broaden the fast food market

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.920
to include salads made
with fresh ingredients.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.240
But building the infrastructure

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.193
and logistics to accomplish
this goal hasn't come cheap.

00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:29.529
- We're not that fancy yet.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.740
- They've always sort
of branded themselves

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.010
as a tech company,

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.720
and so they talked a lot about

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.250
changing the food system.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.540
At one point they said that they wanted

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.000
to be the McDonald's of better eating.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.410
Now they've had to translate

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.330
some of those lofty
ambitions into reality,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.190
and that's challenging.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.760
- [Narrator] This is The
Economics of Sweetgreen.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.550
Sweetgreen brought in hundreds of millions

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.910
in investment before going
public in November 2021.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.860
In an SEC filing, it reported having

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.130
about 1.35 million active customers.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.350
After its IPO, its stock surged

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.380
to bring the company's
value to over $6 billion.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.550
- I'm obsessed.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.560
- [Narrator] But its
market cap has since fallen

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.720
to almost one quarter of that.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.360
While individual Sweetgreen
locations are profitable,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.350
the company has struggled to
overcome high overhead costs.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.950
In its last quarterly report,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.360
the company announced net losses

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.550
of more than $27 million.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.410
- Hi, what can I get
started for you to eat?

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:25.980
- [Narrator] The company's
costs begin with its salads.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.290
- There's a few things that
drive the cost of what we do.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.560
We buy really, really high quality food

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.270
from farmers we know and trust.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.620
- [Narrator] Most
restaurants source their food

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.450
through distributors,
which give them access

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.030
to a wide range of food at low prices.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:39.930
And on top of that,

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.110
these distributors handle
the transportation logistics.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:46.710
Sweetgreen, on the other hand,
works directly with farms.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.500
Another major cost is labor.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.660
Sweetgreen has staff assemble meals

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.020
and also do a significant
amount of food prep.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.600
- Most restaurants process
their food centrally

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.250
and ship it out around the country.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.460
In order to maximize the
taste and the freshness,

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.620
we believe food should be made closer

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.450
to where the guests are eating the food.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.370
So we actually make our food

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.100
every day in our fresh prep kitchen.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.870
- [Narrator] Beyond
restaurant level expenses,

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.380
Sweetgreen has also put a
lot of money into technology.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.140
- We've built out from just
having a pickup channel,

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.730
to building our own native delivery,

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.620
partnering with some marketplaces,

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.650
and even building catering
and our outpost business.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.450
We've also been able to integrate

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.480
machine learning and AI
in order to personalize

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.250
a lot of the recommendations
that we give you,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.710
as well as things like
our loyalty program.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.780
- Sweetgreen hasn't just
built tech for customers,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.790
it's also built apps for employees

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.350
to plan out how much food to make

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.760
at different times of day,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.090
so food is fresh but ready
when they expect customers.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.650
- I would say that the founders

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.810
are trying to be more disciplined now.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.390
They've also earned a lot
in stock compensation,

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.010
and I think there is certain amount

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.020
of tech alignment thinking there.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.630
But you know, they are
coming down to earth a bit

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.030
and trying to trim expenses

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.430
where they can and try
to become more efficient.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.620
But again, it's gonna take time.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.270
- [Narrator] The question
is how to do that

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.470
without changing the parts

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:10.080
of the business that customers care about.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.370
- Our path to profitability

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.010
in a net income basis
comes from a few levers.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.290
The first is continuing
to grow our footprint.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.900
This year, we're opening
about 35 new restaurants.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.230
Second is growing sales in existing stores

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.990
where a huge portion of that increase

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.200
goes to lifting the profitability
of those restaurants.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.030
The third is being very disciplined

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.370
on our cost structure to make sure

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.140
that the incremental profit we're making

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.640
is flowing through the bottom line.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.440
- [Narrator] Sweetgreen
has closed some restaurants

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.360
in cities like Boston and New York.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.580
It's also had some layoffs.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.600
- One of the challenges

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.750
for the business has
clearly been the pandemic

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.751
and the recovery from the pandemic.

00:03:48.751 --> 00:03:50.520
- [Narrator] In 2019, Sweetgreen stores

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.770
were concentrated in urban centers,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.270
but recently it's been focused

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.370
on expanding outside cities.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.360
- I think we're going to continue

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.680
to build out in the markets

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.660
that we currently operate in,

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:01.710
and looking to open up

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:05.130
one or two new markets a year
for the next several years.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.270
- [Narrator] Sweetgreen recently hired

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.860
two former Chipotle executives

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.120
to help make its menu appeal

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.070
to a wider range of customers,

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:14.160
especially as it expands
past major cities.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.530
That's important because
its path to profitability

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.850
centers on having enough

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.760
profitable restaurants to offset overhead.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.650
To make each restaurant more profitable,

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.630
it's also counting on increasing loyalty

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.820
and leveraging technology.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.750
Sweetgreen has experimented

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.430
with loyalty programs for years,

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.600
and its most recent effort

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.610
is something called Sweetpass.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.290
There are a few tiers in the program.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.670
In the paid version of Sweetpass,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.380
customers pay $10 per month

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.380
to get $3 off one salad per day.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.120
So a customer would have to spend

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.810
at least $40 on salads per
month to come out ahead.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.730
- In general, restaurants
are really pushing

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.810
these loyalty programs

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.460
because it makes a lot of sense

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.630
to try to get someone hooked.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:53.010
You know, it's harder to advertise

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.750
to a new customer than it is to try

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.730
to just keep current one coming.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.350
But you know, if you're going to eat that

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.480
every day for lunch, that is gonna add up.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.590
- [Narrator] Sweetgreen hasn't shared

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.760
how many people have signed up

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.970
for its loyalty program, which
it still considers a pilot.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.850
Another key strategy moving
forward is automation.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:11.820
In 2021, Sweetgreen bought Spyce Food Co,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.460
a startup that makes
automated food assembly lines.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.570
And earlier this year,

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.090
it opened its first
so-called Infinite Kitchen

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.530
in Naperville, Illinois,

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:21.900
where salads are assembled robotically.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.840
That enabled it to hire
one third fewer staff

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.630
without sacrificing efficiency.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.590
Sweetgreen plans to continue

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.270
rolling this out to new locations,

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.230
and hopes to retrofit an
existing location in late 2024.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.520
- Probably the biggest improvement

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.400
for our customers is
much faster throughput.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.350
Typically, you can order your salad

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:42.540
and have it ready in under three minutes,

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.400
even in a very busy store.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.080
- We believe what this will allow us to do

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.780
is provide a superior economic model.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.970
This will significantly impact

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:53.190
and improve our unit economics,

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.260
which will allow us to continue

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.730
to scale in a profitable way,

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:00.390
and over time may even
give us some pricing power

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.250
as we think about creating healthy food

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.650
that is truly accessible for everyone.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.330
- [Narrator] Sweetgreen
has made some progress

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.440
towards profitability.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.760
Last quarter, the company announced

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.710
it was profitable for the first time,

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.050
though this comes with
some qualifications.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.460
Sweetgreen is only profitable

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.900
based on a measure called EBITDA,

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.100
which excludes a variety

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.590
of costs such as taxes, acquisition costs,

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.500
restructuring costs, and
stock-based compensation.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.600
It's a measure that's
popular with tech companies,

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.240
but doesn't follow generally
accepted accounting principles.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.400
- It's a pretty heavy list of things

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.760
that aren't included, but by doing this,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:33.720
I mean, they can say that

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.030
they just had their
first profitable quarter,

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:39.390
which is in Q2, and they wanna show

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.860
some progress to investors.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.720
And I think that does show

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.400
a certain magnitude of progress,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.900
but it's not all the way there.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.520
- [Narrator] The company
though is confident

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.320
that it can become a national business

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.030
based on three things.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.280
It creates a new category in the market,

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.990
has capital to expand,

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.450
and maintains a loyal customer base.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.430
- We see Sweetgreen as having all three

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:01.830
of those ingredients as we move forward.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.120
- You know, I think there will continue

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.800
to be challenges as we scale,

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.450
whether it be how we
scale our supply chain,

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.010
how we scale our technology,

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.750
how we scale our leadership.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.400
But I think the big thing is proving

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.050
that this type of offering

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.790
can work all around the country.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:15.900
- I think they're pretty honest

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.100
that they're trying to become

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.410
a more mature business now.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.450
And you know, for a young company

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:22.770
founded by young founders,

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.293
that makes sense that
that's a little bumpy.

00:07:26.606 --> 00:07:29.856
(gentle upbeat music)

